nuinely uncertain.", "watch": "Independent or nonpartisan polling confirming or contradicting the Democratic-sponsored surveys would most move this forecast.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Mike Carey (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Ohio's 15th District, which leans about five points Republican, has unexpectedly become competitive. Incumbent Mike Carey, first elected in 2021, faces Democrat Don Leonard, a first-time candidate who has narrowed the gap in polling since mid-September. The most recent survey, from a Democratic-affiliated pollster in mid-October, showed Leonard up three points after he trailed by five in June. Outside groups have poured roughly $6.5 million into the Columbus-area contest, and Leonard has kept pace despite Carey's fundraising and cash advantages.\n\nAnalysts mostly rate the race Lean Republican, though a couple call it a tossup, and prediction markets give Leonard roughly a one-in-three chance. The combination of an incumbent, a right-leaning electorate, and a favorable national environment for Democrats leaves the result genuinely uncertain, with Carey holding a modest edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1732, "margin": -5.63}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.185, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1905, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1541, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1527, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1532, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1445, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1885, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.341, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.336, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3468, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2931, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.3015, "margin": -3.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2475, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2324, "margin": -4.